Column Type Null Key/Default Purpose <code>org_id</code> UUID no FK→organisations (cascade), idx Parent firm <code>office_id</code> str(32) yes UNIQUE with <code>org_id</code> (nulls not distinct) JQ's office identifier, or <code>NULL</code> for the firm-level DEFAULT card. A firm may have one DEFAULT card plus one card per named office (multi-office pricing); the portal only edits the DEFAULT card and search only consumes the DEFAULT card until office-level portal editing/search ships (issue #64) <code>price_type</code> enum no <code>estimated</code>/<code>verified</code>/<code>no_data</code> (default <code>no_data</code>) Drives the estimated-price uplift; <code>no_data</code> ⇒ <code>quote = null</code> in results, ranked last, not top-5 eligible. Sourced from the Price tab's Verified / Estimated / Unavailable column (<code>Unavailable</code>/<code>No data</code> both map to <code>no_data</code>) <code>pricing</code> JSONB no <code>{}</code> Anchor fees + modifiers + additional costs + disbursements (shape below) <code>source</code> str(10) no <code>import</code> Provenance of the current card: <code>import</code> (Master Export) vs <code>portal</code> (firm self-service edit) <p><code>pricing</code> JSONB shape (built by <code>scripts/import_master_export.py</code>, consumed by <code>price_calc.py</code>):</p> <pre><code>{
  "freehold":  { "purchase": {"150000": 950, ... "1500000": 1450}, "sale": { ... } },
  "leasehold": { "purchase": { ... }, "sale": { ... } },     // 7 anchors each: 150k,250k,500k,750k,1m,1.25m,1.5m
  "modifiers": [ {"name": "Acting for lender", "amount": 150}, ... ],              // 16 rows, imported verbatim
  "additional_costs": [ {"name": "SDLT submission fee", "amount": 80}, ... ],      // 5 rows, imported verbatim
  "disbursements": [ {"name": "Disb - searches (CML standard pack)", "amount": 350,
                      "estimated": true, "vat_applies": false}, ... ],
  "anchor_states": { "freehold_purchase": {"150000": "unavailable", ...}, ... }
}
</code></pre> <p>Sentinel Price-tab cells (<code>Unavailable</code> / <code>Not Offered</code> / <code>Withheld</code>) are recorded in <code>anchor_states</code> per tenure/side rather than as a numeric fee; the anchor lookup then has no fee for that cell.</p> <p>Every named <code>modifiers</code>/<code>additional_costs</code> row on the current (07.07.26) Master Export is imported verbatim, whether or not <code>price_calc.py</code> currently applies it — see §6 for which rows are wired into a trigger.</p>
